      "text": "Service layer",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "center",
      "verticalAlign": "middle",
      "containerId": "wWGQ_p_EmwQj6GQ8hy6BL",
      "originalText": "Service layer",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "kupv-5YK5uLzUMgMD1ahb",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 305.0727289373223,
      "y": 2529.418182373047,
      "width": 1067.8193359375,
      "height": 400,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "#b2f2bb",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b0D",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 302530637,
      "version": 874,
      "versionNonce": 968990477,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1779214791137,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "4. Service layer is responsible for implementing all the core algorithms and business logic. Serivce layer \ndon't directly interact with the database. \n\n5. Repositories are the set of code which is having only one responsibility, to interact with the DB. \nThey have your actual queries and function which will be executed on the db server. \n\n6. schema/models how the data in the db looks like\n \n7. Migrations folder keep the changes happening in ur SQL db\n\n8. Helper functions go in the utils folder\n\n9. DTO -> Data transfer objects -> contains the definition of what objects is transfered over the network \nvia diff models/schema\n\n",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "4. Service layer is responsible for implementing all the core algorithms and business logic. Serivce layer \ndon't directly interact with the database. \n\n5. Repositories are the set of code which is having only one responsibility, to interact with the DB. \nThey have your actual queries and function which will be executed on the db server. \n\n6. schema/models how the data in the db looks like\n \n7. Migrations folder keep the changes happening in ur SQL db\n\n8. Helper functions go in the utils folder\n\n9. DTO -> Data transfer objects -> contains the definition of what objects is transfered over the network \nvia diff models/schema\n\n",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
